# .trivyignore — review-approved exceptions for the trivy image CVE gate.
#
# Policy (AUT-1749): the base-image scan (.github/workflows/trivy-image-scan.yml)
# fails on HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs that have an upstream fix. Only CVEs listed here are
# tolerated, and each MUST carry a justification + the PR/issue that approved it.
# Prefer a digest bump over an ignore entry whenever a fixed image exists.
#
# Format: one CVE id per line (leading `#` = comment; empty lines ignored).
#
# Example (do NOT ship blind suppressions — only add a CVE after confirming it is
# not exploitable in our usage and the CTO/security reviewer has signed off):
# CVE-2024-0000  # accepted: bookworm-slim base, no network-exposed listener; review AUT-XXXX

# --- AUT-1749: pgvector/pgvector:pg17 gosu-stdlib CVEs -----------------------
# Source: the `gosu` binary (GOSU_VERSION=1.19) bundled in the postgres image.
# trivy attributes Go stdlib CVEs to it (package "stdlib", Go 1.24/1.25). gosu
# is used ONLY to drop privileges before exec'ing postgres — it performs no
# network/TLS/URL/XML/MIME/HTTP2 processing, so none of these are reachable in
# AutoBrain's Postgres data-store role. Confirmed: the pinned pg17 digest has
# ZERO postgres/debian HIGH|CRITICAL CVEs; all 22 findings are gosu-stdlib.
# Flagged for security-reviewer acknowledgement on PR #306 (AUT-1749).
CVE-2025-61726  # gosu-stdlib: net/url; unreachable in privilege-drop helper
CVE-2025-61729  # gosu-stdlib: net/url; unreachable
CVE-2025-68121  # gosu-stdlib: crypto/tls cert validation; gosu does no TLS
CVE-2026-25679  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable in privilege-drop helper
CVE-2026-27145  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-32280  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-32281  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-32283  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-33811  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-33814  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-33818  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-39820  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-39821  # gosu-stdlib: idna/punycode; gosu does no DNS
CVE-2026-39822  # gosu-stdlib: os.Root symlink; gosu exec's a fixed target
CVE-2026-39836  # gosu-stdlib: net NUL byte; unreachable
CVE-2026-42499  # gosu-stdlib: net/mail; gosu parses no mail
CVE-2026-42504  # gosu-stdlib: mime; unreachable
CVE-2026-56853  # gosu-stdlib: net/http HTTP/2; gosu does no HTTP
CVE-2026-56858  # gosu-stdlib: html/template; unreachable
CVE-2026-56859  # gosu-stdlib: encoding/xml; unreachable
CVE-2026-56860  # gosu-stdlib: net/url; unreachable
CVE-2026-56862  # gosu-stdlib: crypto/tls KeyUpdate; gosu does no TLS

# --- AUT-1735 / python base image HIGH CVEs (unused at runtime) ------------------
# Both findings are pip packages present in the python:3.13-slim base image
# (PYTHON_BASE_IMAGE). grep across the repo + PyPI metadata confirms NEITHER
# msgpack nor setuptools is imported or invoked by any AutoBrain runtime service
# (backend/ai/worker/market-data), so neither is reachable:
#   * msgpack: no `import msgpack` anywhere; kombu/celery/redis only require it
#     via OPTIONAL extras that are NOT installed; celery serializer is pinned to
#     json (backend/app/workers/celery_app.py: task_serializer/accept_content/
#     result_serializer="json"), so kombu never imports msgpack at runtime.
#   * setuptools: no runtime `import setuptools`/`PackageIndex`; packages are
#     installed at build, never fetched via PackageIndex at runtime.
# Re-verified 2026-10-02 (AUT-4718) against python:3.13.16-slim-trixie@sha256:6906dca8...:
# still msgpack 1.1.2 and setuptools 70.3.0, i.e. no python tag respin has shipped
# msgpack>=1.2.1 / setuptools>=78.1.1, so suppress per policy ("tolerate when no
# fixed image exists"). Time-boxed: re-check 2026-11-28; drop entries + bump
# PYTHON_BASE_IMAGE digest once a respin ships them. At that re-check,
# ALSO re-run `grep -rnE 'import msgpack|from msgpack|PackageIndex'` across the
# repo AND scan the FINAL built images (not just the bare base), so a future
# reachable msgpack/PackageIndex usage cannot hide behind this ignore.
# Security Officer sign-off: APPROVED (AUT-1844). Both IDs per advisory are listed
# below (GHSA + CVE aliases) so a trivy DB refresh that leads with the CVE cannot
# silently re-break the gate.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  # msgpack OOB read/crash on Unpacker reuse: NOT imported; unreachable
CVE-2026-57585  # msgpack: CVE alias of GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (same advisory); unreachable
CVE-2025-47273  # setuptools PackageIndex path traversal: build-time only, no runtime install path
GHSA-5rjg-fvgr-3xxf  # setuptools: GHSA alias of CVE-2025-47273; build-time only

# --- AUT-1793 / python base image OpenSSL QUIC DoS -----------------------------------
# CVE-2026-14456: OpenSSL DoS via unbounded memory growth in QUIC server, fixed in
# 3.5.7-1~deb13u2. Re-verified 2026-10-02 (AUT-4718): python:3.13.16-slim-trixie
# @sha256:6906dca8... ships openssl/libssl3t64 3.5.7-1~deb13u3 on BOTH amd64 and arm64,
# so this finding no longer reproduces and no entry is carried (it is already absent).
# AutoBrain never enables QUIC in any OpenSSL consumer (FastAPI/Uvicorn, celery
# worker, market-data, ai gateway all use TLS ≤1.3 over TCP/HTTPS). QUIC exposure
# requires explicit openssl ctx set_quic_method() calls none of our stacks perform.
# Re-added to .trivyignore after AUT-1794 removed the prior entry; same justification.
# Time-boxed: re-check 2026-11-28; drop entry + bump PYTHON_BASE_IMAGE digest once
# a 3.13-slim respin ships openssl>=3.5.7-1~deb13u2.

# --- AUT-1998: nginx libexpat HIGH CVEs — RESOLVED by the AUT-4718 digest bump ---------------
# RESOLVED (AUT-4718, 2026-10-02): the pin moved to
# nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:stable-alpine@sha256:ed04ec1f... (Alpine 3.24.2), which
# carries libexpat 2.8.5-r0 on both the amd64 and arm64 manifests (verified by
# extracting lib/apk/db/installed from every layer of both manifests). That is
# >= the fix for CVE-2026-66046 / CVE-2026-76641 (2.8.4-r0) and CVE-2026-93990
# (2.8.5-r0). Entries DROPPED, not re-suppressed. libexpat-version-check.yml
# THRESHOLD raised to 2.8.5-r0 and its PINNED_DIGEST synced to ed04ec1f.


# --- AUT-2762 / AUT-2332 / AUT-1600-PR: nginx util-linux + placeholder CVEs — RESOLVED (AUT-4718) ---
# RESOLVED (AUT-4718, 2026-10-02): all of these cleared when the nginx pin moved to
# @sha256:ed04ec1f... (Alpine 3.24.2, libuuid 2.42.3-r1). A clean scan of that digest at
# HIGH/CRITICAL with an EMPTY ignorefile returns zero util-linux/libuuid findings and
# zero CVE-2026-80256, so the 15 suppression lines are DROPPED rather than carried
# forward. They were hiding nothing, but they would have masked the next real finding.

# --- POSTGRESQL libpcre2 CVEs (pgvector/pgvector:pg17) ---
# CVE-2026-86145 / CVE-2026-89161: pcre2 out-of-bounds write + JIT memory corruption.
# Source: libpcre2-8-0 10.42-1 in the pgvector/pgvector:pg17 (debian 12.15) base image.
# Fixed in 10.42-1+deb12u1 (already published by Debian). The pgvector upstream
# image has not yet been rebuilt with the patched pcre2 package. Suppress until
# the pgvector:pg17 image digest is refreshed; re-check 2026-11-30. Postgres
# reaches pcre2 only via server-side regex operators (~, ~*, POSIX regex) on
# user-queried columns; AutoBrain's backend does not expose raw regex input to
# end-users on any public API endpoint (AUT-2918).
CVE-2026-86145  # pcre2 OOB write: not exposed via public API regex input
CVE-2026-89161  # pcre2 JIT memory corruption: same exposure surface as above

# --- AUT-4718: pcre2 32-bit-only OOB write, same deb12u1 upstream fix -----------
# CVE-2026-89157: pcre2_pattern_convert out-of-bounds write when an attacker
# supplies a large pattern. Debian security-tracker describes it as affecting
# 32-BIT PLATFORMS ONLY ("PCRE2 before 10.48, on 32-bit platforms, ..."). Every
# AutoBrain container image is amd64 or arm64 (64-bit); the pgvector:pg17 digest
# we pin has no 32-bit variant in the deploy path, so the vulnerable code path
# cannot execute here. Same source package/fix as the deb12u1 entries above:
# libpcre2-8-0 10.42-1 -> 10.42-1+deb12u1, pgvector image not yet rebuilt.
# Re-check 2026-11-30 with the entries above: drop when the pgvector:pg17 digest
# ships deb12u1. Security Officer sign-off: APPROVED (AUT-4718).
CVE-2026-89157  # pcre2 pcre2_pattern_convert OOB write: 32-bit platforms only; we run 64-bit

# --- AUT-2918: python base image gzip/libsqlite3/perl-base CVEs — RESOLVED (AUT-4718) -------
# RESOLVED (AUT-4718, 2026-10-02): the pin moved from python:3.13.15-slim-trixie
# (@sha256:9d2e5553...) to python:3.13.16-slim-trixie (@sha256:6906dca8...), which carries
# Debian 13.7 point-release packages that fix all ten: gzip 1.13-1+deb13u1,
# libsqlite3-0 3.46.1-7+deb13u2, perl-base 5.40.1-6+deb13u1. Verified by scanning the new
# digest at HIGH/CRITICAL with an empty ignorefile: zero gzip, libsqlite3-0 or perl-base
# findings. Entries DROPPED, not re-suppressed.

# --- AUT-4718: pcre2 CVE-2026-103111 (OOB write, attacker-controlled regex + JIT) ---------
# "PCRE2 before 10.49, when there is an attacker-controlled regular expression and certain
# JIT API usage, allows an out-of-bounds write with arbitrary data."
# (GHSA-r9hj-j2rw-4q3m). Two conditions must BOTH hold, and neither is reachable here:
#
#   1. Attacker-controlled regular expression. AutoBrain compiles no regex from user input
#      on any request path. The only regexes in the runtime are literals in our own source
#      and in docker/frontend/nginx.conf (the one PCRE location is the static
#      `location ~ ^/(autobrain-assets|autobrainservice-assets)/` prefix match). No public
#      API endpoint accepts a pattern string (established for AUT-2918 and unchanged).
#   2. JIT API usage. The python base image links NO pcre2 into the interpreter: the
#      CPython binary's DT_NEEDED list is exactly {libc.so.6, libpython3.13.so.1.0}, and
#      Python's `re` is the bundled `_sre` C module, not pcre2. libpcre2-8-0 is present
#      only as a dependency of libselinux1. nginx's PCRE is used for location matching with
#      static patterns and the image ships no JIT-enabled pcre2 build for our config.
# Sources: pcre2 10.48-r0 (nginx Alpine 3.24.2) and libpcre2-8-0 10.46-1~deb13u2 (python
# Debian 13.7). Fixes ARE published upstream — Alpine 3.24 main carries pcre2-10.49-r0 and
# debian-security carries libpcre2-8-0 10.46-1~deb13u3 — but neither nginxinc nor the
# python image has been rebuilt with them, so no digest bump clears this today. Suppress
# per policy ("tolerate when no fixed image exists").
# Time-boxed: re-check 2026-11-30; drop the entry and bump the nginx + python base digests
# as soon as either upstream image ships the fixed pcre2. Re-run the DT_NEEDED and
# nginx.conf checks at that point so a future dynamic-regex or JIT path cannot hide here.
CVE-2026-103111  # pcre2 OOB write: needs attacker-controlled regex + JIT; neither is reachable

# --- AUT-4718: urllib3 CVE-2026-97687 / CVE-2026-97689 (pip's vendored copy) ----------------
# urllib3 2.7.0 ships ONLY inside pip's vendor tree — `usr/local/lib/python3.13/
# site-packages/pip/_vendor/urllib3/` — and pip's own lock file records `urllib3==2.7.0`.
# There is no top-level urllib3 dist-info in the image, so this is pip's private copy, not
# an installed dependency of any AutoBrain service.
#   * CVE-2026-97687 (HIGH, traffic interception via HTTPS proxy TLS config override): pip
#     is invoked only at image build to install requirements.txt from PyPI. No
#     HTTPS_PROXY is configured in the build, and no runtime process executes pip.
#   * CVE-2026-97689 (HIGH, DoS via unbounded allocation in the chunk parser): reachable
#     only by feeding a crafted HTTP response to pip's own downloader at build time.
# AutoBrain's runtime HTTP stack is httpx (pinned 0.28.1 in backend/ and ai/), which does
# not use urllib3; `grep -rn urllib3` across backend/, ai/, worker/, market-data/ and every
# requirements.txt returns nothing. Runtime urllib3 CVEs are covered by the pip-audit
# resolved-tree gate (AUT-1189), which is green.
# Fixed in urllib3 2.8.0, but pip 26.2.1 (the version in every current python tag) still
# vendors 2.7.0, so no image bump clears this. Suppress per policy.
# Time-boxed: re-check 2026-11-30; drop both entries once a python tag ships a pip that
# vendors urllib3 >= 2.8.0, and re-verify that no requirements.txt gained urllib3.
CVE-2026-97687  # urllib3 proxy-TLS override: pip's vendored copy, build-time only; runtime uses httpx
CVE-2026-97689  # urllib3 chunk-parser DoS: pip's vendored copy, build-time only; runtime uses httpx
